{"data":[{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.1","text":"I laud Agni, the chosen Priest, God, minister of sacrifice, The Hotar, lavishest of wealth.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1#:~:text=I%20laud%20Agni%2C%20the","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.2","text":"Worthy is Agni to be praised by living as by ancient seers: He shall bring hitherward the Gods.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.3","text":"Through Agni man obtaineth wealth, yea, plenty waxing by day, Most rich in heroes, glorious.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.4","text":"Agni, the perfect sacrifice which thou encompassest about Verily goeth to the Gods.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.5","text":"May Agni, sapient-minded Priest, truthful, most gloriously great, The God, come hither with the Gods.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1#:~:text=May%20Agni%2C%20sapient%2Dminded%20Priest%2C","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.6","text":"Whatever blessing, Agni, thou wilt grant unto thy worshipper, That, Angiras, is indeed thy truth.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.7","text":"To thee, dispeller of the night, O Agni, day by day with prayer Bringing thee reverence, we come;","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.8","text":"Ruler of sacrifices, guard of Law eternal, radiant One, Increasing in thine own abode.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1","urantiaParallels":[]},{"work":{"id":"rig-veda","title":"The Hymns of the Rigveda","tradition":"Hindu"},"reference":"RV 1.1.9","text":"Be to us easy of approach, even as a father to his son: Agni, be with us for our weal.","url":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Hymns_of_the_Rigveda/Book_1/Hymn_1#:~:text=Be%20to%20us%20easy","urantiaParallels":[]}]}